  "body": "IP NAS 1.0.0: the Raspberry Pi 5 NAS, its screen, Nur Hub and the Nur app.\n\nDownloads\n- `ipnas-panel-1.1.0.bin`: firmware for the case screen (ESP32-S3).\n- `nur-android.apk`: Nur for Android.\n- `nur-windows-x64.zip`: Nur for Windows (unzip and run `nur.exe`).\n- `nur-linux-x64.tar.gz`: Nur for Linux.\n- Nur Hub runs on the NAS from Docker Hub: `multix00/nur-hub:1.2.0` (also `latest`), for arm64, armv7 and amd64.\n\nWhat Nur needs before the first chat\nNur runs AI models on your own NAS with llama.cpp. The app walks you through it and does not open the chat until all three are done:\n1. Pair the app with Nur Hub on the NAS.\n2. Install llama.cpp on the NAS (Nur Hub runs it as a Docker container).\n3. Download a model. Only models that fit your NAS's RAM are listed, and the smallest one that works well is recommended.\n\nAfter a download, and every time Nur Hub or llama.cpp starts, Nur Hub loads the model and reads Nur's system text in the background, so the first chat does not wait for it.\n\nEvery answer is written by the model. If a tool or the NAS fails, Nur shows the error instead of a reply. When the NAS is off or not reachable, the app says so.\n\nWeb search uses SearXNG on the NAS. Nur Hub turns on its JSON output by itself and keeps checking until SearXNG is installed.\n\nOllama is not supported. Nur works with llama.cpp only.\n\nPlease read the [disclaimer](https://github.com/MultiX0/ip-nas/blob/main/DISCLAIMER.md): small local models make mistakes and can be slow.\n"
